WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.880
Replacement Razor cartridges sell for $5 when five blades and their plastic housing can be stamped and assembled for under 30 cents. This is First Principles Daily, episode 102. The difference is not hidden in exotic alloys or rare materials. It sits in the way the product is designed, protected and sold. Cartridge razors reached their current form through incremental additions rather than wholesale redesign. Each new blade count was layered onto an existing handle interface

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.140
that competitors could not legally copy.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.560
The handle itself became the lock.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.660
Once a user owned the handle,

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:39.680
every future purchase had to match its geometry.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.580
Manufacturers therefore shifted attention

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:44.500
from lowering the cost of the cartridge

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.100
to extending the period between purchases.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:50.540
Subscription services and multi-packed pricing

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.760
made the per-unit cost feel smaller,

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.440
even as the absolute margin stayed high.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.100
Retail shelf space and brand advertising

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:02.900
advertising further reinforced the sense that $5 was the normal price for a month of

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:03.320
shapes.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.660
Inside the factory, the process remains conventional.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:12.160
Thin, stainless strip is stamped into blades, edges are ground encoded, and the blades

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.360
are captured in a molded plastic housing.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:19.800
These steps are fast and repeatable, yet the final assembly still travels through a supply

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:23.480
chain built around patent protected interfaces and marketing budgets.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:30.060
The result is a finished item whose selling price bears little relation to the cost of its constituent materials.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:37.980
One objection sometimes raised is that the blades themselves must carry hidden expense because of precision grinding and edge coating.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:47.160
In practice, the grinding uses standard abrasive wheels on continuous strip and the coating is a thin PTFE layer applied in a single pass.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:52.880
Both operations run at high speed on the same line that stamps the blades, so their incremental

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.080
cost stays low.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:59.720
Another common point is that regulatory or safety testing adds substantial overhead.

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:05.840
Ed sharpness and skin contact standards exist, yet they are already satisfied by the lowest

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:08.140
cost private label blades on the market.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:11.960
Compliance itself does not require the observed price gap.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:17.460
app. The dominant cost-lakers therefore remain outside the press and the mold. They include

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:22.280
the legal defense of handle geometry, the advertising that sustains brand perception,

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:27.920
the slotting fees paid for shelf position, and the commissions taken by subscription platforms.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:33.560
Each layer compounds because the product moves through multiple intermediaries before reaching

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:38.840
the user, and each intermediaries margin is calculated on the inflated selling price

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:52.800
rather than on the material value. If a magic wand could instantly arrange the raw atoms into finished blades in housing, the cost would be set by commodity prices for stainless steel strip and polypropylene or ABS plastic.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:03:00.780
A set of 5 blades uses perhaps a few grams of steel. At current commodity values that steel is worth only a few cents.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:06.340
sense. The plastic housing adds another few cents. Adding modest allowances for coatings

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:11.080
and packaging still leaves the total raw material value well below 30 cents.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:17.760
Dividing the observed retail price of $5 by that 30 cent floor produces an idiot index

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:24.240
in the range of 15 to 20. In other words, the finished cartridge costs roughly 15 to 20 times

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:29.280
the value of the materials it contains. Most of that multiplier does not come from the

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:34.280
stamping or grinding operations themselves. It accumulates in the steps that sit between

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:39.540
the press and the checkout scanner. Those steps include patent filings and legal defense,

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:44.860
brand advertising, retail slotting fees, subscription platform commissions,

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:48.880
and the carrying cost of inventory held at every point in the chain.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:54.300
Each of these layers is accepted as normal because the product has always been sold this way.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:04:00.260
The steel in plastic could be formed in a single high-speed line that feeds directly into low-cost

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:05.480
distribution. Nothing in the physics of cutting hair requires the layers of distribution and

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:11.040
protection that now sit on top of the blades. The high idiot injects therefore signals an

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:17.040
opportunity located in the business architecture rather than in the metallurgy. To test the floor

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.360
More carefully, consider the steel alone.

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:26.440
Commodity 301 or 304 stainless strip, suitable for blades, trades in the range of a few

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:27.320
dollars per kilogram.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:33.880
Five blades weighing roughly 2 grams each total 10 grams, so the steel value sits well

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:36.960
under 5 cents even before any processing credit.

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:44.540
The plastic housing, typically injection molded polypropylene or ABS, adds another 3-5 cents

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:45.520
at pellet prices.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:51.140
Edge coding and simple cardboard or blister packaging contribute a further few cents.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:55.180
Summing these gives the same sub-30 cents ceiling you used earlier.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:05:01.800
The gap to $5 is therefore not explained by material volatility or by any exotic input.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:07.740
It is explained by the sequence of legal, marketing and channel steps that sit after the physical

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:08.620
part is complete.

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:13.380
A redesign would begin by separating the blade edge from the handle interface.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:19.420
Standard, non-proprietary cartridges could be produced at commodity scale and sold through

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:21.200
any retailer or direct channel.

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:26.900
The first concrete move would be to publish an open mechanical specification so that multiple

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:29.440
manufacturers could supply compatible blades.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:32.300
Next would come process consolidation.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:38.720
Feed steel strip and plastic pellets into one automated cell that stamps, grinds, assembles,

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:41.160
and packages without intermediate inventory.

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:46.120
That change removes several handling steps and their associated carrying costs.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:49.320
The harder constraints are legal and perceptual.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:55.400
Existing patents on handle geometry would have to expire or be designed around, and users

00:05:55.400 --> 00:06:00.220
would need to accept that a lower priced cartridge does not automatically mean a lower quality

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:00.620
shave.

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:06.500
Safety standards for edge sharpness and skin contact would still apply, yet those standards

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:10.020
are already met by low cost, private label blids sold today.

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:15.660
The remaining barrier is therefore mainly the willingness to treat the cartridge as a standardized

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:22.080
consumable rather than a proprietary accessory. An open specification might reduce incentives

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:28.420
for quality improvement. In practice, commodity stainless blades already demonstrate consistent edge

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:34.780
life across multiple suppliers once the geometry is fixed. Differentiation would then shift to measurable

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:40.500
attributes such as coding durability or blade count rather than to proprietary handle locks.

00:06:41.240 --> 00:06:46.620
Retailers might resist losing the high margin refill business, yet the same retailers already

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:52.200
stock low-cost private label blades that achieve comparable performance at a fraction of the branded

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:57.340
price. Channel acceptance is possible once the product is decoupled from the handle.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:03.860
The sequence of moves therefore starts with the open specification proceeds to integrated high-speed

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:08.560
manufacturing, and then relies on expiration or circumvention of the remaining

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:13.540
interface patents to open volume distribution. When the price of a simple

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:17.400
assembly is set by the shape of its handle, rather than the cost of its

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:21.060
steel, the opportunity lies in questioning the handle itself.

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:26.240
Treating the blade as a standardized commodity forces every other cost into the

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:30.700
open where it can be attacked one layer at a time. The first signal that

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:32.420
that someone is attempting the Razer case

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:34.740
would be an open mechanical specification

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:38.120
published alongside a prototype produced at commodity cost.

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:41.300
That's a wrap on today's first principles breakdown.

